<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-atholl"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/duke-of-atholl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Duke of Atholl</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Duke of Atholl is a title in the peerage of Scotland created in 1703 for John Murray, Marquess of Atholl.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-aveiro"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/duke-of-aveiro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Duke of Aveiro</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Duke of Aveiro was a Portuguese ducal title created in 1535 for João de Lencastre, a grandson of King John II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/duke-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Duke of Saxony</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Duke of Saxony was the ruler of the duchy of Saxony in the Holy Roman Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-shao"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/duke-of-shao.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Duke of Shao</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">The Duke of Shao, personal name Ji Shi, was a senior member of the Zhou royal house who helped King Wu overthrow the Shang.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/duke-of-zhou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Duke of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">The Duke of Zhou, Ji Dan, was a brother of King